# xlgr highlighting rules: one per line, first match wins for each property.
#
#   /regex/[i]  attribute...
#
# The regex is POSIX extended (use [0-9] or [[:digit:]], not \d). Attributes:
#   fg=COLOR bg=COLOR   X colour name or #rrggbb
#   bold underline      text styles
#   dim                 fade the text colour towards the background
#   group=N             colour only parenthesised group N (default: whole match)
#   line                colour the whole line when the regex matches anywhere
# A "#" token starts a comment.

/^[0-9:.]+ /          fg=gray50                 # leading timestamp
/(ERROR|FATAL|PANIC)/i  fg=white bg=red bold line
/WARN(ING)?/          fg=#b06000 bold
/\<0x[0-9a-f]+\>/i    fg=blue                   # hex numbers
/heartbeat|keepalive/ dim line                  # quiet noise
/\[([a-z_]+)\]/       group=1 fg=#006060        # [module] tag
